# @puranderdua8/tokens and @puranderdua8/theme are published to GitHub
# Packages from the `web-components` repo. Only these two are consumed as
# installed packages — the UI components themselves arrive as source via
# `npx shadcn add`, and are never installed from a registry.
#
# The auth token deliberately does NOT live here. pnpm refuses to expand
# environment variables in registry credentials read from a project-level
# .npmrc, because that file is committed and a malicious registry entry
# could otherwise exfiltrate the token. Put it in your user-level ~/.npmrc:
#
#   pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken" <your-pat>
#
# CI sets the same key from secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN — see .github/workflows/ci.yml.
@puranderdua8:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
